    ["Train by fighting with any supported combat style. Constitution progresses alongside combat.", "Use Harmony to resupply between trips. The Combat training Atlas list helps you move up from low-risk targets to longer fights."],
    ["Start with an equipable bow and matching ammunition. Train at Lumbridge chickens or goblins.", "Advance to Falador cows, then try Rock Crabs or other Atlas combat routes. Keep an eye on ammo and bring food for tougher targets."],
    ["Use bones from normal combat to start. Hill giants are a later source of big bones.", "For later training, the Atlas lists the Hefin cathedral and cleansing crystals at suggested level 75. Prifddinas access and the activity's own checks still apply."],
    ["Choose an unlocked spell in your spellbook, equip a compatible weapon and bring runes.", "Start in Lumbridge with a low-level target. On an eligible Ironman, the Ironman staff covers runes for supported combat and utility spells through level 55. Level and spell access checks still apply."],
    ["Cook basic fish or meat on an accessible range. Cook's Assistant opens access to the Lumbridge castle range.", "Use Al Kharid or another bank-side range for larger batches. Gather raw fish in Fishing to train both skills."],
    ["Start with normal trees near Lumbridge, then move to bank-side oaks in Draynor.", "Bring an axe and use the later Atlas routes to find other trees. Keep the logs for Fletching, Firemaking or Construction as appropriate."],
    ["Start with a knife and normal logs for basic shafts or bows.", "Use Draynor's bank and woodland for the oak and willow stages. Keep a stock of bowstrings and the correct ammunition parts when needed."],
    ["Start with a small net in Draynor or Al Kharid. Bring a rod and bait for the relevant spots.", "Pick a bank-side route for raw food you want to keep. The spot's tool, bait and level requirements still apply."],
    ["Bring a tinderbox and start with ordinary logs in a clear area.", "Draynor offers a bank-side route for the oak and willow stage. Save the logs you need for other skills before burning a batch."],
    ["Start at the Lumbridge castle spinning wheel with wool or flax.", "Later, look at the Ithell harps for harmonic dust once you meet the route and access requirements. Use material chains such as spinning flax for Fletching supplies."],
    ["Start with copper and tin at the Lumbridge furnace, then use the nearby anvil for bronze work.", "Al Kharid offers a later furnace route. Bring the correct ore, coal and tools for each recipe, and compare using your bars versus selling them."],
    ["Start at the Lumbridge swamp copper and tin mine with a pickaxe.", "Use the Atlas to find higher-level ores and plan the bank trip. Keep copper and tin for bronze Smithing if you need both skills."],
    ["Check Druidic Ritual first, then use the Taverley route for beginner supplies and potion preparation.", "Gather vials, herbs and recipe secondaries. Train with potions you will actually use, and check each recipe's own level."],
    ["Run complete laps in obstacle order at Burthorpe or the Gnome Stronghold.", "Use the later course listings as you qualify. A suggested route level does not override quest, location or obstacle checks."],
    ["Start on men or women in Lumbridge. Harmony's starter stall is another local route.", "Ardougne offers several stall tiers. Check the actual stall requirement, leave room for rewards and watch for guards."],
    ["Choose a master in the Harmony courtyard and accept a task.", "Use the on-screen task panel's Teleport to task when available. Prepare for the assigned target rather than treating a nearby training area as the assigned location."],
    ["Start at the Falador or Catherby allotments. Bring seeds and the tools to clear and plant the patch.", "Work herb, allotment and flower patches into a route. Bring compost when appropriate, and use the crop's planting level."],
    ["Start at the air altar ruins with essence and the appropriate talisman or tiara.", "Move to the mind altar and other listed altars as your level allows. Bring the correct essence type and entry item for the chosen altar."],
    ["Start with the bird and kebbit areas in Feldip using the appropriate snares or traps.", "The Piscatoris route adds other targets as you qualify. Check the target's required tool before travelling."],
    ["Start at a house portal such as Rimmington and enter your own house.", "Use building mode and gather the materials for the furniture you plan to build. Other portals still depend on relocation and access."],
    ["Bring the charm, empty pouch, spirit shards and secondary ingredient to a Summoning obelisk.", "Taverley is a listed starting route. The Summoning shop supplies materials, while charms come from eligible gameplay drops."],
    ["Start at Daemonheim and form a party or enter with a solo party.", "Play the available floors and check floor unlocks as you advance. Floor rewards follow Dungeoneering's rules, so use actual completion awards to plan progress."],
    ["Start on pale wisps near Draynor and convert the memories at the local rift.", "Move to flickering wisps in Falador as you qualify. Check whether you want energy, XP or a combination before converting."],
    ["For the first Veilmarket visit, walk to the graveyard south of Lumbridge church.", "Use a death guard and skull lantern you can equip. Check the Atlas Veilmarket entry for access and supplies, then use beginner combat areas to practise."]
